# FABLE-SONNET-DECL-PREPASS-20260923-137 part 2 into an explicit reference (the sibling of
# unit_struct_return_assign_refused, whose held Structure is callable): `@: Model b` is a typed reference, and
# `b: other(a)` binds it only after the admission of the call's result to Model (OPUS-CALLABLE-STRUCT-BINDING-
# 20260929-16).  other returns an Other of another shape (two ints, no size_t in value's place): the admission refuses
# it, the method's implicit throw `implements`, uncaught, stops R0.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

Other:
    int: p 1
    int: q 2
end: Other

fn: other (Model: x) Other
    t: merge Other
    return: t
end: other

fn: probe () int
    a: merge Model
    @: Model b
    b: other(a)
    return: 7
end: probe

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: probe(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
